WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
So how do you think your relationship to the festival has changed throughout the years?

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:09.900
So, now that you’re the actual artist of the poster versus just going and selling some of your art.

3
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:16.620
Well, the poster and Jazz Festival are two separate entities.

4
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:24.500
So, Jazz Festival hasn’t always honored the poster artist.

5
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:38.780
You know, most festivals you go to, if you’re doing the poster, then they’ll accommodate you and kind of almost put you on a pedestal.

6
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:46.700
Well, because Jazz Festival subcontracts another company to take care of that,

7
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:56.260
they haven’t always recognized the artist, so . . . And okay, well that’s fine.

8
00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.220
So, but what I’ve had to do over the years is kind of say, “Hey, listen.

9
00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:12.880
I’m doing the poster, and just like your musicians are bringing a crowd and generating income or profit for you, the artist, in the same way,

10
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:23.940
is bringing a crowd and generating a profit for you, so, can I get two weekends?” [laughs] You know, or, “Can you waive my booth fee?”

11
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:32.840
Or you know, just . . . That was the relationship at first, but now it’s a lot better.

12
00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:42.140
And so, now I get two weekends, and I’ve managed to get my own booth.

13
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:51.080
Whereas before, I had to—even if I did the poster—I had to share booths or a tent, at least, with other artists.

14
00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:59.000
And it’s cool because now I know that by speaking up about it, I changed it.

15
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.240
And so, now, every artist that does a poster has his own booth and has two weekends from here on out.

16
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.860
So, that’s probably the major difference.
